* ===========================================================================
*  Speaker demo in MOL80: a C-major scale and a high beep, played on the (guessed) one-channel
*  speaker.  See crates/cpt-machine/src/speaker.rs for the port interface:
*      port 128  divisor LOW byte   (latched only)
*      port 129  divisor HIGH byte  (commits {high, low} and starts the tone)
*      tone frequency = 1,000,000 / (2 * divisor) Hz;  divisor 0 = silence
*
*  Hear it:
*      cargo run -q -p mol80asm -- --bin speaker/melody.bin speaker/melody.mol
*      cargo run -q -p cpt-run -- --steps 5000000 --speaker-wav melody.wav speaker/melody.bin
*  then open melody.wav.
*
*  Each note sounds for NOTELEN, then the speaker is silenced for GAPLEN so repeated notes are
*  distinct.  A divisor of 0 in the table ends the tune.  The CPU just waits in a delay loop
*  while the tone generator does the work.
* ===========================================================================
SPKLO     EQU 128
SPKHI     EQU 129
*  DELAY costs 24 cycles per pass: 20833 passes = 500,000 cycles = 250 ms at 2 MHz.
NOTELEN   EQU 20833
GAPLEN    EQU 2500
*
          ORG 0
          /START
*
          ORG 100H
START     NOTES:HL
NEXT      (HL):E
          HL+1:HL
          (HL):D
          HL+1:HL
          D:A
          A-*E:A
          FZ=1? /DONE
          E:A
          A:PORT(SPKLO)
          D:A
          A:PORT(SPKHI)
          NOTELEN:BC
          CALL(DELAY)
          0:A
          A:PORT(SPKLO)
          A:PORT(SPKHI)
          GAPLEN:BC
          CALL(DELAY)
          /NEXT
*  Interrupts are off after reset, so this HLT is terminal: the emulator stops.
DONE      WAIT
*
*  DELAY: wait BC passes of a 24-cycle loop.  Clobbers A and BC.
DELAY     BC-1:BC
          B:A
          A-*C:A
          FZ=0? /DELAY
          RTN
*
*  Divisors for C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5, then a 1250 Hz beep, then the 0 terminator.
NOTES     DW 1911, 1703, 1517, 1432, 1276, 1136, 1012, 956, 400, 0
